        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 88-year-old female patient, admitted on 22/08/1990 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed signs of airway obstruction. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. She was promptly treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and close monitoring of vital signs. Her condition improved satisfactorily, and she was discharged in a stable condition. Pulmonary rehabilitation and patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management were initiated. Please arrange close follow-up. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information. Kind regards, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
